  "contribution": {
    "summary": "Independently qualify the six completed M2 phases and twelve task contracts, run eight new cross-layer IR/composition tests and all composition/IR/quantities/foundation regressions, package three locked local Math NuGets, verify each manifest's dependency graph and SHA-256, then compile and execute an isolated .NET 10 NuGet-only consumer before closing the M2 milestone.",
    "value": "A verified local preview of bounded typed IR and deterministic provider-neutral exact composition with reproducible exact replay, independent of AURA and from direct project references, can be consumed through transitive NuGet packages.",
    "debtChanges": [
      "M2 closure covers the accepted preview only; M3 numerical algorithms, M4 symbolic algorithms, M5 interoperability and external AURA adoption remain open/planned.",
      "Structural hashes are canonical tree identities, not algebraic equivalence proofs; binary64 cross-platform bit-for-bit portability remains unqualified.",
      "NuGet artifacts are verified local ignored outputs with observed SHA-256, not publicly published or installed in AURA.",
      "Provider description, versioned identity and local replay do not grant provider execution, AURA permission or remote/distributed service guarantees.",
      "RS038 retry 0 failed before attempt allocation: authoring preflight refused direct filesystem mutations and JsonArray.Add in the C# payload. Retry 1 stages a separate NuGet-only consumer via the Payload SDK, uses an AOT-safe JSON array factory, and preserves the same six-phase M2 gate.",
      "A persistent, standalone NuGet-only smoke-consumer fixture under tests/consumers is installed by the typed Payload SDK and excluded from the solution; its restore is restricted to the locally generated package feed.",
      "RS038 retry 1 failed before attempt allocation (payload-compilation, CS0119 at payload.cs line 146): the NuGet-only consumer version comparison used the undeclared Version symbol, resolved as System.Version. Retry 2 binds the explicit CompositionVersion constant without changing the accepted M2 gate, fixtures, or mutation scope."
    ],
    "nextAction": "After qualified M2 gate success, inspect DWF milestone transition and prepare the next substantial admissible M3-W01-C01 phase from its accepted backlog; keep M3 scientific scope and independent RED/GREEN evidence bounded.",
    "achievements": [
      {
        "projectNode": "M2",
        "achievement": "The M2 six-phase preview gate is qualified by complete native/product evidence, eight independent cross-layer contract tests, full local regressions, a locked three-package NuGet dependency graph with observed hashes, and a clean isolated consumer; M3 and external AURA adoption are not claimed."
      }
    ]
  },
